Re-notify writable fallback readiness after the bounded selector wait.

Suppressing continuously writable descriptors entirely prevents a tight event-
port loop, but it can also strand Tokio writers after their earlier readiness
has been consumed. This is visible when Codex negotiates with the code-mode
host successfully, then waits forever before writing a later request to the
same pipe.

Keep transition notifications in the pre-wait fallback check. In the post-wait
check, report writable readiness again even when it remains set. The event-port
wait still limits this to once per fallback interval, preserving liveness
without restoring the busy loop.

